    "title": "Spurs vs. Warriors: How to watch the game, who's starting, who's out",
    "text": "San Antonio Spurs center Victor Wembanyama, right, drives to the basket against Golden State Warriors center Quinten Post during the first half of an NBA basketball game in San Francisco, Wednesday, Feb. 11, 2026. (AP Photo/Jeff Chiu)Jeff Chiu/Associated PressSpurs (57-18) vs. Warriors (36-39)When/where: 9 p.m. Wednesday at Chase Center, San Francisco.Article continues below this adTV/radio: ESPN; 1200 AM, 1350 AM (Spanish), 107.5 FM (Spanish).Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢PROBABLE STARTERSSpurs: PG De'Aaron Fox (6-3, 9th year), SG Stephon Castle (6-6, 2nd); SF Devin Vassell (6-5, 6th), PF Julian Champagnie (6-7, 4th), C Victor Wembanyama (7-4, 3rd). Warriors: PG De'Anthony Melton (6-2, 8th), G Brandin Podziemski (6-4, 2nd), SF Gui Santos (6-7, 3rd), PF Draymond Green (6-6, 14th), C Kristaps Porzingis (7-2, 11th).RESERVESSpurs: G/F Keldon Johnson (6-6, 7th), G Dylan Harper (6-6, 1st), C Luke Kornet (7-1, 9th), F Harrison Barnes (6-7, 14th), C Bismack Biyombo (6-8, 15th), G Lindy Waters III (6-5, 5th), C/F Kelly Olynyk (6-11, 13th) G Jordan McLaughlin (6-0, 7th), F Carter Bryant (6-6, 1st), C Mason Plumlee (7-0, 13th). Inactive: Luke Kornet (right knee injury management), David Jones Garcia (right ankle surgery), Harrison Ingram (two-way), Emanuel Miller (two-way).Article continues below this adWarriors: G Seth Curry (6-1, 13th), G Pat Spencer (6-2, 3rd), G Will Richard (6-3, 1st), G Gary Payton II (6-2, 10th), G Nate Williams (6-5, 4th), C Quinten Post (7-0, 2nd), G LJ Cryer (6-0, 1st), F Malevy Leons 6-9, 2nd, C Omer Yurtseven (6-11, 4th). Questionable: Richard (left heel soreness). Inactive: Jimmy Butler III (right ACL surgery), Stephen Curry (right patellofemoral pain syndrome), Al Horford (right soleus strain), Moses Moody (left patellar tendon surgery).COACHESSpurs: Mitch Johnson.Warriors: Steve Kerr.STAT LEADERSSpurs: Points, Wembanyama (24.5 per game). Rebounds, Wembanyama (11.4). Assists, Castle (7.2). Steals, Castle/Fox (1.2). Blocks, Wembanyama (3.1).Article continues below this adWarriors: Points, Porzingis (13.3 per game). Rebounds, Green (5.5). Assists, Green (5.4). Steals, Richard (1.2). Blocks, Green (0.6).NOTABLE• Stephen Curry has missed 25 games in a row with a balky right knee. The Warriors are 9-16 in that stretch and 13-23 overall this season in games he has missed. • Wednesday's game is the first in the final back-to-back of the season for the Spurs. They are 23-5 in back-to-back situations, including 12-2 in the first game, with both losses coming on the road.Article continues below this ad• Wembanyama has ripped down 15 or more rebounds in four consecutive games to tie the longest streaks of Tim Duncan and David Robinson in their Hall of Fame careers. Dennis Rodman holds the franchise record with seven streaks of 15-plus games (longest nine in a row).Tom OrsbornSan Antonio Express News LogoTake your fandom to the next level with breaking news, in-depth reports and expert analysis.",
